## 🎯 What are ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs?

ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs are a lightweight, “bottom‑up” way to build HTTP APIs without the boilerplate of controllers, routing attributes, and even `Startup.cs`.  
They were introduced in **.NET 6** (and remain in .NET 7/8) to let you:

| Traditional MVC | Minimal API |
|------------------|-------------|
| `Controller` + `Action` methods | Plain C# delegate / lambda |
| Lots of attribute routing (`[HttpGet]`, `[Route]`) | `app.MapGet("/path", handler)` |
| XML/JSON configuration | Simple, fluent configuration |
| `Startup.cs` + `ConfigureServices` / `Configure` | Single `Program.cs` (or minimal `Startup`) |

> **Why use them?**  
> • Faster to prototype or build small services.  
> • Less code, fewer files.  
> • Full access to DI, middleware, health checks, Swagger, etc.  
> • Great for micro‑services, serverless functions, or quick experiments.

---

## 🚀 Quick‑Start: Create a Minimal API

### 1. Create a new project

```bash
dotnet new web -n MinimalTodoApi
cd MinimalTodoApi
```

`dotnet new web` creates a project with *Program.cs* that already contains a minimal template.

### 2. Open `Program.cs`

You’ll see something similar to this after the template:

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
var app = builder.Build();
app.MapGet("/", () => "Hello World!");
app.Run();
```

Let’s transform this into a simple **To‑Do** API.

### 3. Add a model

```csharp
public record TodoItem(int Id, string Title, bool IsCompleted);
```

### 4. Create a fake in‑memory store

```csharp
var todos = new List<TodoItem>
{
    new TodoItem(1, "Learn Minimal APIs", false),
    new TodoItem(2, "Build a real app", false)
};
```

### 5. Register Swagger (optional but handy)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddEndpointsApiExplorer();
builder.Services.AddSwaggerGen();
```

### 6. Add endpoints

```csharp
app.MapGet("/todos", () => todos);

app.MapGet("/todos/{id:int}", (int id) =>
{
    var todo = todos.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == id);
    return todo is not null ? Results.Ok(todo) : Results.NotFound();
});

app.MapPost("/todos", (TodoItem newTodo) =>
{
    // Simple ID generation
    newTodo = new TodoItem(todos.Max(t => t.Id) + 1, newTodo.Title, newTodo.IsCompleted);
    todos.Add(newTodo);
    return Results.Created($"/todos/{newTodo.Id}", newTodo);
});

app.MapPut("/todos/{id:int}", (int id, TodoItem updatedTodo) =>
{
    var index = todos.FindIndex(t => t.Id == id);
    if (index == -1) return Results.NotFound();

    todos[index] = updatedTodo with { Id = id };   // keep same ID
    return Results.Ok(todos[index]);
});

app.MapDelete("/todos/{id:int}", (int id) =>
{
    var removed = todos.RemoveAll(t => t.Id == id);
    return removed > 0 ? Results.Ok() : Results.NotFound();
});
```

### 7. Enable Swagger UI

```csharp
if (app.Environment.IsDevelopment())
{
    app.UseSwagger();
    app.UseSwaggerUI();
}
```

### 8. Run

```bash
dotnet run
```

Open `https://localhost:5001/swagger` (or `http://localhost:5000/swagger` depending on your Kestrel binding) to interact with the API.

